<title>UK: Clarke says stg, low cost pressures help RPI.</title>
<headline>Clarke says stg, low cost pressures help RPI.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said subdued cost pressures and the stronger pound were helping to curb inflation.</p>
<p>Commenting on December retail price data, he said:</p>
<p>&quot;These figures show that subdued cost pressures and a stronger pound are feeding through to lower inflation.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Richard Murphy, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
</text>
